  "note": "The unique principal Muzibu Azaala Mpanga royal tomb exterior:complete broad curved thatched shell with naturally hanging near-soil hem,plain small apex cap/finial,a wide low arched entrance cut into the roof with actual recessed depth,closed dark reed/timber backing,closed ceiling/jamb reveals and earthen entry floor. Sparse original reed/timber framing and geometric lower thatch bundles. Independent gate,drum-house,court,royal-family houses and30-hectare estate remain native;no generic substitute model,no navigable interior or graves. PMTiles principal footprint is29.86 by30.16m,area681.4m2,no height tags or inner hole. Circular roof diameter30.3m,crown12.1m,plain finial12.98m,12m wide entrance rising2.95m above a0.6m entry floor andback plane9.2m are ordinary-picture proportions,not surveyed dimensions. Datum1238m is rounded current standard field elevation;natural outer hanging hem follows that unchanged field plus0.18m. Entry level is an approximate reasonable visualization threshold,not a historic survey. +X SSW along the courtyard facade;+Z WNW toward the forecourt/general monument point;+Y up. Provisional picture/courtyard reconstruction,not surveyed facing."
